# InvestPal ecosystem credentials.
#
# `make setup` writes .env.secrets from this template at mode 600. Nothing here
# is required — the Claude Code cockpit works with every value blank.
#
# The Claude Code agent is denied read access to .env.secrets by the
# permissions.deny rules in .claude/settings.json. Keep credentials in this
# file rather than in .env, which the agent may read.
#
# Note the limits of that: these values are exported into Claude Code's own
# process environment by `make claude`, because .mcp.json interpolates them into
# request headers and the broker MCP servers accept credentials no other way.
# The deny rules stop a stray file read, not a determined one.

# ── LLM provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only for InvestPal's own backend agent (the /chat REST endpoint, the Streamlit
# dev UI, backend-run workflows). The cockpit does not need a key: there,
# Claude Code is the LLM. Supply the one matching LLM_PROVIDER in .env.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ── Alpaca (stocks and ETFs) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paper-trading keys by default; see ALPACA_API_BASE_URL in .env.
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_API_SECRET=

# ── Coinbase (crypto) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COINBASE_API_KEY is the key *name*. The secret must be base64-encoded.
COINBASE_API_KEY=
COINBASE_API_SECRET=

# ── Market data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Entirely optional: the data sources work without a key. This only raises
# CoinGecko's rate limits.
COIN_GECKO_API_KEY=

# ── Turso Cloud sync ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when TURSO_SYNC_URL is set in .env.
TURSO_SYNC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Interactive Brokers has no entry here on purpose: it authenticates through a
# browser login to its own gateway, never with an API key.
